      ":question/id": "d724ae77-2273-56ab-852e-2415e473e7f8",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-13840",
      ":question/problem": "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{2}}\\frac{2}{5x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}).$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\cdot 2x=\\frac{2}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $e$ | ${e}^{2}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{2}}\\frac{2}{5x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{2}}\\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{2}{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|){|}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡{2}^{2}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
